    "reviewer": "claude-code S339",
    "findings": [
      "S339 CANON-053 pass. Inspected home in dark and light at 1366px and the tier sections at 1366px and 390px. CONFIRMED FIXED: the doubled status label on the hero tiles is gone -- one pill per tile, and the bare clipped 'S' on the narrow tiles is gone with it. Root cause was not markup: build-game-covers.mjs rasterized the status word into every cover, directly under where .hero-tile__badge is absolutely positioned, and background-size:cover clipped it on narrow tiles. A Playwright DOM probe found exactly one status node per tile, which is what ruled out markup and client-side injection and pointed at the asset (D-S339.6). CONFIRMED FIXED: the Sparked tier now shows all five products the canonical feeds call SPARKED (Call of Doodie, Franchise Architect, PromoGrind, Velaxis, Vorn); Velaxis and Vorn were previously filed under Forge. No per-card status badge remains in any tier, and a stray 'Sparked' meta chip on Franchise Architect -- found on the rendered capture AFTER the badge rule was already green -- was removed and gated. KNOWN AND CARRIED, not a regression: the cover artwork still renders the genre eyebrow and the title beneath the tile's own live kicker and name, so those two remain doubled; it reads as a layered lockup at featured size and as a smudge at tile size, and is on the board as [S339][UX/P3] to be decided as a design question rather than patched per breakpoint. Capture caveat: the full-page matrix catches the hero lede mid-reveal, so lede opacity in those frames is an animation artifact and not a contrast defect; the tier captures settle the reveal before shooting."
    ],
    "fixesApplied": [],
    "blockingDefectsOpen": 0,
    "limitation": null
  },
